{
  "description": "Labelled raw-JSON acceptance/rejection RULE TABLE for the published catalogue boundary (unit 1d-c2b1). Explicitly NOT a snapshot and NOT a query result: it is a RULE TABLE whose expected envelopes and decoded values are handwritten literals, never computed by an implementation. Every raw document is preserved as a STRING inside this valid table JSON, so malformed lexemes survive intact.",
  "raw_json_rule": "Raw JSON validation runs BEFORE any structural schema check. An intended raw failure yields one literal envelope: exactly ok+error, ok strictly false, error exactly code+message = invalid_json / Invalid catalogue JSON. Every integer token is checked EXACTLY, before any precision-losing conversion, against [-9007199254740991, 9007199254740991]; floating/exponent tokens convert with normal binary64 semantics and reject nonfinite or integer-valued results outside that range, so unsafe integers reject in every notation. Duplicate member names reject at EVERY object nesting (including decoded escape-equivalent keys); a name repeated in two separate objects is fine and different case is distinct. MAX_JSON_DEPTH is 64 inclusive: a root container is depth 1, each nested array/object adds 1, both kinds count, a root scalar is depth 0, and quoted brackets never count. Strict JSON syntax is required with no BOM stripping, trimming or sanitizing.",
